    {
      "eval_id": "E002",
      "user_id": "U-002",
      "user": "Rahul Sharma",
      "question": "What was the root cause of the BluePeak Electronics inventory synchronisation drift on 19 May 2026?",
      "category": "authorized_factual",
      "expected_behavior": "answer",
      "actual_behavior": "answer",
      "status": "PASS",
      "answer": "**Root cause**\n\nThe drift was caused by **two independent faults acting together**:\n\n- The nightly stock batch scheduler applied a fixed **UTC offset** while the stock window was computed in **IST**.  \n- A **stale SKU‑mapping table** left over from the March catalogue restructure was still being consulted by the pipeline.  \n\nNeither fault alone would have breached the six‑hour freshness requirement, but together they produced up to **26 hours** of inventory synchronisation drift (Project Status Report PRJ‑S002‑003; Incident Report INC‑2026‑0519; Support Ticket TKT‑2026‑0519‑207).\n\nSources:\n- Project Status Report PRJ-S002-003 - Page 1\n- Incident Report INC-2026-0519 - Pages 1, 2\n- Support Ticket TKT-2026-0519-207 - Pages 1, 2, 3",
